<http://data.silknow.org/object/1d5923f3-6eb1-3e60-85db-df8cc54b403a>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Brocaded silk damask cover. The cover has a deep salmon pink ground brocaded with silver-gilt thread and coloured silks. It has a pale blue lining and a border of gilt braid. There are two widths of material in the width of the cover. The design consists of a vertical stem of exotic fruit and leaves in bunches. The brocaded silk details alternate between red and two shades of blue. There are two repeats of the design in the width of the material.\n\n<u>Technical details</u>\nSatin of 5 ground, the pattern being in reverse damask. The pattern is bound in 3/1 twill by a proportion of warp threads taken from the ground warp. 2 kinds of metal thread, frisé and filé (used in paired shoots)."@en , "Brocaded silk damask cover, French, 1710-20."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/aed961a9-e253-315e-97db-fa183275e0d4> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Brocaded silk damask cover. The cover has a deep salmon pink ground brocaded with silver-gilt thread and coloured silks. It has a pale blue lining and a border of gilt braid. There are two widths of material in the width of the cover. The design consists of a vertical stem of exotic fruit and leaves in bunches. The brocaded silk details alternate between red and two shades of blue. There are two repeats of the design in the width of the material.\n\n<u>Technical details</u>\nSatin of 5 ground, the pattern being in reverse damask. The pattern is bound in 3/1 twill by a proportion of warp threads taken from the ground warp. 2 kinds of metal thread, frisé and filé (used in paired shoots)."@en , "Brocaded silk damask cover, French, 1710-20."@en ;
